{
    "_comment": [
        "Maps POS product SKU to the product slug on shuddhidham.com, so image sync",
        "attaches the right photo every run. The two catalogues share no key: POS is",
        "keyed by SKU, the website by slug, and web names carry Devanagari. Matching",
        "on names at runtime would eventually hang the wrong photo on a product, so",
        "the pairing is decided once, here, by a human.",
        "Two SKUs may point at one slug (e.g. premium/standard figs share a photo).",
        "SKUs under no_web_product have no counterpart on the website; they are listed",
        "so the reason is recorded and the question is not reopened every sync."
